# Weight Watchers

> Weight Watchers (WW) is a global health and wellness company offering science-backed weight-loss programs, nutrition guidance, coaching, and clinical solutions including GLP-1 medication support. WW operates across 15 markets.

## How It Works

Weight Watchers uses a proprietary **Points Program** that assigns values to foods based on their nutritional content — higher sugar and saturated fat increase Points, while protein and fiber lower them. Members receive a personalized daily Points Budget that adapts as their body changes.

Plans include:
- **Core** — The foundational program with the Points system, food tracking, activity tracking, and access to the WW app with recipes and coaching.
- **Core+** — Everything in Core plus live coached Workshops (virtual and in-person) for community support and accountability.
- **GLP-1 Support** — Programs designed for members taking GLP-1 medications, with clinician-guided journeys, medication tracking, and a dedicated Care Team (clinicians, fitness coaches, registered dietitians). Availability varies by market.

